    "chunk_text": "Amaratunga also claimed that, through the intervention of another senior port official, the matter was brought to the attention of Deputy Minister of Ports Janitha Kodituwakku, who had instructed him to lodge a complaint with the Criminal Investigation Department.\n\nThe businessman further alleged that the CID, the Mirihana Financial Crimes Division, the Fort Police, the Peliyagoda Financial Crimes Division and the Central Crimes Investigation Division had all refused to accept his complaint.\n\nHe has therefore requested the Bribery Commission to conduct a full investigation into all individuals allegedly connected to the incident, including officials attached to the Managing Director\u2019s office, the Supply Division and the Finance Division of the Ports Authority.\n\nCopies of the complaint have also been forwarded to the President, the Minister of Ports and Aviation Services, the Chairman of the Ports Authority and seven other parties, the complaint stated."
