    "chunk_size_bytes": 1808,
    "chunk_text": "The Healthcare sector delivered a strong performance in FY26, recording revenue of Rs. 37.4 billion, a 14.9 percent YoY increase. The performance was driven by the pharmaceutical agency, distribution, retail, and medical devices businesses, reflecting the sector\u2019s strong operational base and continued market penetration.\n\nHealthguard Distribution posted revenue growth of 25.2 percent YoY, supported by the full-year impact of its model change and the onboarding of five new distribution clients. Sunshine Medical Devices recorded revenue growth of 12.3 percent YoY, supported by stable demand across core product categories.\n\nLina Manufacturing recorded a 5.1 percent YoY revenue decline, primarily due to lower prices for Government purchase orders for the 2026 calendar year.\n\nHealthguard Pharmacy, the retail arm of the Group, achieved revenue growth of 11.3 percent, driven by value and volume growth across both pharma and wellness segments.\n\nThe Consumer sector, which includes both export and domestic branded businesses, recorded 2.8 percent YoY revenue growth in FY26 and accounted for 28.9 percent of Group revenue. This performance was supported by continued resilience in the branded tea portfolio and a gradual recovery in the confectionery business.\n\nWithin branded tea, revenue grew by 7.6 percent YoY, supported by strong execution across modern trade channels, which helped drive 8.7 percent YoY volume growth. The Group\u2019s flagship tea brands, Zesta, Watawala, and Ran Kahata, continued to perform across the mass market, value-for-money, and premium segments.\n\nThe confectionery segment recorded 8.5 percent YoY revenue growth and 8.9 percent YoY volume growth, led by strong performance in Gums and Wafers categories, supported by promotional initiatives and wider channel coverage."
  },
