    "language": "en",
    "md5": "3c4a01e6bb8ad6cf5b1a67a3419670c1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1963,
    "chunk_text": "CSE with EU-funded Green Recovery Facility drives SL\u2019s GSS+ bond market\n\nFrom left: SEC Deputy Director General and Officer-In-Charge Tushara Jayarathna, Sustainable Business Specialist (Expertise France GSS+ Bonds Activity Lead) Shayani Weeresinghe, CSE CEO Rajeeva Bandaranaike, Expertise France Lead Project Manager Morgan Rohel and Baastel Consultancy Team Senior Sustainable Finance Expert Jason Taylor\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s sustainable finance market continues to gain momentum as the Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE) collaborated with the European Union (EU)-funded Green Recovery Facility, implemented by Expertise France, to advance the country\u2019s growing pipeline of green, social, sustainable and sustainability-linked (GSS+) bonds through a series of targeted market-building programmes earlier last month.\n\nThe CSE collaborated with the EU-funded Green Recovery Facility implemented by Expertise France on a combined training-of-trainers (ToT) programme and a C-suite keynote session with a focus on incentivising potential issuers and investment banks for GSS+ bonds earlier this month, in addition to a separate ToT programme for independent external verifiers and investors aimed at strengthening the enabling environment for a pipeline of GSS+ bonds.\n\nThe EU Green Recovery Facility is a EUR 5 million initiative, which began in 2023 and was implemented by Expertise France and aims to bring about economic opportunities through sustainability practices, driving both growth and resilience. The facility facilitates action on sustainable energy, climate action and sustainable finance, by undertaking education programmes with governments and businesses to identify key actions, stimulate innovation and unlock sustainability-aligned public and private sector investment.\n\nA key focus of this initiative has been strengthening the sustainable finance ecosystem, including the development of the GSS+ bond market and a mechanism for national coordination."
  },
