    "md5": "33d68a0d3b007a879587b4868a523256",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1947,
    "chunk_text": "Hayleys surpasses half-trillion revenue milestone in FY 2025/26\n\nThe Hayleys group recorded the highest revenue in its history during the financial year ended March 31, 2026, with a 19 percent year-on-year increase to Rs.585.02 billion.\n\nThe consolidated profit before tax rose by 4 percent to Rs.38.04 billion. The performance gathered momentum in the fourth quarter, with revenue increasing by 29 percent to Rs.164.62 billion and profit before tax improving by 6 percent to Rs.13.87 billion.\n\nEvery sector contributed positively to the operating earnings, driven by the domestic businesses benefiting from the favourable market dynamics and export-oriented sectors demonstrating resilience.\n\nThe operating environment remained supportive, reflecting the macroeconomic stability, accommodative monetary conditions and private sector credit growth.\n\nWhile the latter part of 2025 was impacted by Cyclone Ditwah, economic activity recovered during the fourth quarter, supported by the reconstruction efforts and resilient domestic demand. Globally, the geopolitical tensions caused uncertainty, supply chain disruptions and volatility in the energy markets. Contd. on\n\nThe revenue growth was driven primarily by the consumer and retail sector, which recorded a 44 percent increase to Rs.156.74 billion. The group\u2019s export-oriented sectors collectively recorded a revenue growth of 14 percent.\n\nThe consolidated earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation increased by 8 percent to Rs.64.82 billion, while the earnings before interest and tax rose by 2 percent to Rs.49.37 billion. Consequently, profit after tax amounted to Rs.22.22 billion for the year.\n\nFollowing the completion of a Rs.9 billion rights issue, the group strengthened its capital base to pursue investments and facilitate the partial settlement of debt. Fitch Ratings reaffirmed the group\u2019s National Long-Term Rating at \u2018AAA (lka)\u2019, with a Stable Outlook."
  },
