    "chunk_text": "A dedicated online platform will be available for both exhibitors and foreign visitors/trade buyers, offering free registration and enabling seamless virtual engagement and collaboration, allowing participants to connect, network, and conduct business from anywhere in the world, and complementing this digital accessibility, the exhibition\u2019s dedicated sector segmentation ensures more focused networking and direct access to targeted buyers, creating stronger and more meaningful business opportunities for exhibitors across both physical and virtual platforms.\n\nWith strong participation expected from Government institutions, private sector organisations, international brands, and trade delegations, INFRACON 2026 aims to foster collaboration across the infrastructure and construction sectors and position Sri Lanka as a regional hub for infrastructure development, while further strengthening industry-wide partnerships.\n\nINFRACON 2026 is more than an exhibition, it is a knowledge sharing and networking platform that supports Sri Lanka\u2019s vision for resilient, sustainable and future-ready infrastructure, where visitors will have the chance to engage with exhibitors through live demonstrations, product launches, and interactive displays showcasing modern, sustainable construction solutions, along with several panels discussions that will take place during INFRACON 2026, covering important and timely industry related topics, with speakers including major private sector players as well as public sector bureaucrats and policy makers.\n\nThe event is also proudly supported by its official sponsors, including Gold Sponsor C.W. Mackie PLC, Silver Sponsors AE Solar and Brantel Lanka Ltd., along with Silver Sponsor and Official PVC Partner Phoenix Super PVC, whose collective contribution further strengthens the industry backing and regional relevance of INFRACON 2026.\n\nINFRACON stands as the definitive platform to connect, build, sustain, and integr